00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,660
Good evening ladies and gentlemen.

143
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:31,000
Today we are honored to have Professor Dreiser from the Johns Hopkins University.

144
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:36,360
He will introduce to us the study of the relationship between health and nutrition

145
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:39,420
utilization. Professor Dreiser, please.

146
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,520
Thank you for your introduction, Kara.

147
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:47,740
Well, the study of the relationship between health and how the body takes in and

148
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:52,240
utilizes food substances can be divided into four distinct eras.

149
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:58,780
The first era began in the 19th century and extended into the early 20th century,

150
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:04,020
when it was recognized for the first time that food contained components that were

151
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:08,860
essential for human function, and that different foods provided different amounts of

152
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:10,520
these essential agents.

153
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:15,980
Near the end of this era, research studies demonstrated that rapid weight loss was

154
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:21,740
associated with nutrition imbalance, and could only be rectified by providing

155
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:25,840
adequate dietary protein associated with certain foods.

156
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:32,500
The second era was initiated in the early decades of the 20th century, and might be

157
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,260
called the vitamin period.

158
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:40,620
Vitamins came to be recognized in foods, and deficiency syndromes were described.

159
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:46,680
As vitamins became recognized as essential food constituents necessary for health,

160
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:51,880
it became tempting to suggest that every disease and condition for which there had

161
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:56,740
been no previous effective treatment might be responsive to vitamin therapy.

162
00:14:57,220 --> 00:15:02,620
At that point in time, medical schools started to become more interested in having

163
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:08,080
their curricula integrate nutritional concepts into the basic sciences.

164
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:13,900
Much of focus of this education was on the recognition of vitamin deficiency

165
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:19,620
symptoms. Herein lay the beginning of what ultimately turned from ignorance to

166
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:23,780
denial of the value of nutritional therapies in medicine.

167
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:29,780
Reckless claims were made for effects of vitamins that went far beyond what could

168
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,500
actually be achieved from the use of them.

169
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:40,220
In the third era of nutritional history in the early 1950s to mid 1960s, vitamin

170
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:42,920
therapy began to fall into disrepute.

171
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:49,720
Together with this, nutrition education in medical schools also became less popular.

172
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:55,240
It was just a decade before this that many drug companies had found their vitamin

173
00:15:55,240 --> 00:16:00,840
sales skyrocketing, and were quick to supply practicing physicians with generous

174
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:02,060
samples of vitamins.

175
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:08,360
Expectations as to the success of vitamins in disease control were exaggerated.

176
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:14,400
As is known in retrospect, vitamin and mineral therapies are much less effective

177
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:20,240
when applied to health crisis conditions than when applied to long -term problems of

178
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:23,980
undernutrition that lead to chronic health problems.

179
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:25,920
And the fourth era.

